SWEET WLAN run E (patch 0150, plan 2026-11-14_oriole-oneshot-2 step W5, boot-arg sweetwlan=7 = run D + rows W15..W17): the CA7 release and the first look at the running firmware, READ-ONLY.
W15: release the CA7 from the halted state W6 left (IOCTL 0x21, out of reset): DHD dhdpcie_bus_download_state(FALSE) ends with si_core_reset(sih, 0, 0) on the CA7 (bcm4389 DHD 865527e
     dhd_pcie.c:10343-10344, core selected at :10200) = _ai_core_reset(0, 0) (aiutils.c:1242-1325 via :1328-1347; UCM_CORRUPTION_WAR not defined): RESET_CTL := 1, IOCTL := 0x3, RESET_CTL := 0,
     IOCTL := 0x1 with the waits of swl_core_reset(); four new ONCE tuples SWT_CAR_* (run 5, need W14), the assert only from IOCTL 0x21 / RESET_CTL 0. A stop inside W15 restores RESET_CTL := 1.
W16: poll the last RAM word (it holds the length token since W12) every 50 ms, at most 100 times (bwfm if_bwfm_pci.c:868-874, OpenBSD 9d8cbe8; DHD 5 s, dhd_pcie.c:13636-13647), each poll after
     the RC-local link precondition; the new value must be a word inside RAM with room for 0x40 bytes (DHD :13698-13699, bwfm :876-877) or the run stops (all-ones: dead; token/0: not up, the
     CA7 wrapper is logged as DHD does at :13700-13705).
W17: read pciedev_shared_t bytes 0x00..0x3F (flags/version at 0, console_addr 0x14, fwid 0x1C: DHD include/bcmpcie.h:358-370; ring_info 0x30: if_bwfm_pci.h:137), the hnd_cons_t header
     (buf 0x08, buf_size 0x0C, idx 0x10: include/hnd_cons.h:60-92, if_bwfm_pci.h:156-158) and at most 2 KiB of the console log, printable bytes only ("SWEET WLAN: fwcon: ..."), now and 2 s later
     (new bytes). Every chip-supplied pointer, size and index is checked against the RAM before use (swl_bp_rd: [0x200000, ram_end - 4], word aligned).
No BAR2 store after W14, no EP Command (bus master) write, no ring, doorbell or host_cap write. The only other stores are cfg 0x84 (0 <-> 0x400000, two reusable tuples SWT_W84_*_E, need W15) for
the reads above 0x400000 and the run A window select. x->done is 64-bit now (34 tuples). The firmware is left running at the end (no restore for a successful release; the chip is reset by the
next power cycle). Tests: shim/wlan_wr_host_test.c rune() (fake firmware), tools/test_wlan_wr_mutants.py. HW-WRITE path: review docs/reviews/0150-wlan-fw-ready-review-fable-*.md.

